From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cinders of Chaos <noreply@cindersofchaos.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:36:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] Name: Cinders Map Editor

Our build is named Cinders Map Editor: window titles, start window,
About dialog, error dialog, in-game preview window, updater window,
map description stamp ("Saved with Cinders Map Editor"; the old stamp
is replaced on save like the other editor stamps), screenshots folder,
user texts that named the editor.

Programs: CindersMapEditor.exe and CindersMapEditorUpdater.exe (CMake
OUTPUT_NAME; the release package script, the updater and its tests
follow). The Windows version resource names the product, the licence
and where the source is.

Settings: organisation Cinders, application CindersMapEditor, so our
build has its own key HKCU\Software\Cinders\CindersMapEditor and its
own application data folder.

About dialog (GNU AGPL-3.0 section 5a): the upstream name, its link and
licence stay; a notice says the program is modified by Cinders of Chaos
since 2026-11 and where the source of each version is.

Behaviour otherwise identical.
